{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalParam","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalParam","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRep"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_rel","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L143-L169","doc":"**The three parameters of a `⟨s_k, s_{k+1}⟩`-orbit satisfy one relation.**\n\nAt distances `p`, `r` and their sum — the only distances that occur across such an orbit\n(`TableauCells.axialDist_succ_swapTableau`, `axialDist_swapTableau_word_left`) — the three\nvalues are not independent:\n\n  `a(p+r)·(a(p) + a(r) - (q - q⁻¹)) = a(p)·a(r)`\n\nThis is `Orbit6.seminormalParam_mul_rel` stated directly on `seminormalParam` rather than on\nthe multiplicative coordinates `x = q^{-2p}`, `y = q^{-2r}`, so it can be used where the\ndistances are read off tableaux rather than chosen.  It is the sole algebraic input the\nbraid relation needs beyond `seminormalParam_add_neg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_mul_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_mul_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L127-L141","doc":"**At a scalar distance the block degenerates: `a(1)·a(-1) = -1`.**\n\nThe two size-`1` eigenvalues `q` and `-q⁻¹` multiply to `-1`, so `1 + a(d)a(-d)` — the\noff-diagonal factor of `seminormalBlock`, and the `d < 0` branch of\n`SeminormalRep.offDiag` — **vanishes** exactly at `d = ±1`.\n\nThis is what makes the smaller orbits consistent.  A size-`1` orbit is a `1 × 1` block\nsitting inside the same uniform entry rule as every other; the rule would supply an\noff-diagonal entry `1 + a(d)a(-d)` for it, and the whole construction only coheres because\nthat entry is zero.  Equivalently: `seminormalBlock` at `a = q` has determinant `-1` and\ntrace `q - q⁻¹`, and is already diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_add_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_add_neg","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L115-L125","doc":"**The two diagonal entries of a size-`2` orbit are `a(d)` and `a(-d)`**, and they sum\nto `q - q⁻¹` — exactly the trace of `seminormalBlock`.  So a size-`2` orbit is the block\n`seminormalBlock q (a d)`, whose lower-right entry `(q - q⁻¹) - a d` is `a (-d)`: the same\nformula read from the partner tableau, whose axial distance is `-d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L92-L100","doc":"**Same-column orbit**: axial distance `-1` gives the eigenvalue `-q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam_one","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L81-L90","doc":"**Same-row orbit**: axial distance `1` gives the eigenvalue `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Seminormal.seminormalParam","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalParam.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**The axial-distance parameter of the seminormal block.**  For an `s_i`-orbit whose\naxial distance is `d`, the `(0,0)` entry of the seminormal matrix of `σ_i` is\n\n  `a(d) = (q - q⁻¹) / (1 - q^{-2d})`.\n\nAt `d = 1` (entries in the same row) this is `q`; at `d = -1` (same column) it is `-q⁻¹`;\nat `d = -2` it is the `(0,0)` entry of the hand-built `(2,1)` matrix `S1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}